From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpu_fdinfo: skip an unreadable fdinfo instead of aborting

find_fd() iterates /proc/<pid>/fdinfo with the throwing
directory_iterator. For a non-dumpable process, such as one with file
capabilities, or one that exits mid-scan, the iterator throws
filesystem_error, nothing catches it, and mangoapp aborts. Use the
error_code overloads so the pid simply reports no fdinfo until the next
rescan.
---
diff --git a/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp b/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp
index 4816786..53cab4f 100644
--- a/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp
+++ b/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp
@@ -16,18 +16,15 @@ void GPU_fdinfo::find_fd()
 
     SPDLOG_TRACE("fdinfo_dir = {}", dir);
 
-    if (!fs::exists(path)) {
-        SPDLOG_DEBUG("{} does not exist", path.string());
-        return;
-    }
-
     // Here we store client-ids, if ids match, we dont open this file,
     // because it will have same readings and it becomes a duplicate
     std::set<std::string> client_ids;
     int total = 0;
 
-    for (const auto& entry : fs::directory_iterator(path)) {
-        auto fd_path = entry.path().string();
+    // Inaccessible fdinfo must not abort mangoapp
+    std::error_code ec;
+    for (fs::directory_iterator it(path, ec), end; !ec && it != end; it.increment(ec)) {
+        auto fd_path = it->path().string();
         auto file = std::ifstream(fd_path);
 
         if (!file.is_open())
